<title>POLAND: Polish wholesale wheat and barley stable, rye up.</title>
<headline>Polish wholesale wheat and barley stable, rye up.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish wholesale wheat and barley prices were stable last week while rye prices rose slightly from the previous week, the Agriculture Ministry said.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>Product    wk to Aug 31   pvs week   six-wk range yr/yr change</p>
<p>Wheat	 62 zl/q	 62 zl/q    62-67 zl/q	72 pct</p>
<p>Rye	   39 zl/q	 38 zl/q    38-44 zl/q	63 pct</p>
<p>Barley	53 zl/q	 53 zl/q    53-58 zl/q	66 pct</p>
<p>Source - The ministry's weekly report compiled by the Polish- American market information and standardisation programme. Zl/q = zloty per quintal. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
